# Uninstall-residue probe — what is left in a profile and a preset root after the manual's uninstall
#
#   node deepblend/tools/uninstall-residue-probe.mjs | tee deepblend/docs/probe-uninstall-residue.log
#
# Taken 2026-09-22 (commercial-readiness ledger C4). What it is evidence for: `install.md` §6, and the
# defect that section had until this reading existed.
#
# WHY IT WAS TAKEN. The manual gave the uninstall as four steps and following them IN ORDER re-installed
# the plugin: `dsh plugin remove` emptied the profile's `dsh.profile.bundles` and `dependencies`, and the
# documented second step — `plugin:install -- --portable` — answered `installed (3 change(s))` and wrote
# both keys back, because that step is an INSTALLER. Every command exited 0 and the reader ended exactly
# where they started. Three more residues were invisible for the same reason (nothing was looking): the
# operator layer this repository writes, the seven `@deepblend/*` links, and the presets — a different
# root entirely, where the manual named ONE directory and the deployer installs every preset in
# `deepblend/presets/`, which is two.
#
# HOW TO READ IT. `BEFORE —` lines are the install; `AFTER —` lines are the residue. The `result:` line is
# derived from the `problems` list, not written by hand (D199: a probe log committed as evidence must not
# state its own conclusion independently of its readings). Exit 0 means the residue table was empty.
#
# The contract layer covers the same tool behaviour against a fixture profile
# (`deepblend/tests/contract/uninstall-residue.test.mjs`); what this adds is a profile created by the real
# launcher plus `dsh plugin remove`, which needs pnpm and therefore cannot live in that layer.

